From 4fba8076bf959e34ec6175c6b85659873f889ae5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 21:33:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01340/11171] [outer-loop] .377 RFT: switch to a 2-3-model
 LADDER + add the trl precondition (operator directive)

Operator: "install trl, update the .377 roadmap to the 2-3-model ladder + add the trl precondition."

trl 1.6.0 installed into the carnot .venv (SFTTrainer for the gold-SFT arm, GRPOTrainer for the
verifier-reward RFT arm; coexists with peft 0.19.1 + transformers 5.10.2, no conflict). Matches the
project's ad-hoc ML-deps pattern (peft/transformers also venv-installed, not in pyproject).

Roadmap (.377) now runs the RFT-vs-SFT contrast across a small-model LADDER instead of one base:
- HEADROOM rung (PRIMARY clean-signal): Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B -- current-gen, above the floor, less
  aggressively post-trained -> most room to show a clean RFT gain.
- STRONG rung (robustness): openbmb/MiniCPM5-1B -- current 1B-class SOTA (Llama-arch, peft-friendly);
  tests whether the mechanism holds on an already-strong base (its SOTA-ness comes from aggressive
  On-Policy-Distillation, which LIMITS headroom -- WHY "SOTA on leaderboards" is the wrong sole
  criterion for a headroom test).
- optional 3rd: Qwen2.5-0.5B (max-headroom) or Qwen3.5-2B (size-trend).
Gate is per-base; RFT>=SFT ACROSS the ladder = robust claim, headroom-only = the gain needs headroom
(itself a finding). exp4079 reports per_base dict. exp4077/4078 preconditions assert the ladder bases
load (HF safetensors, NOT GGUF) + `from trl import SFTTrainer, GRPOTrainer` imports (no silent skip
like the off-ARC runner). All cached, so the ladder adds little wall-clock on sub-1B LoRA.
Verified: parses, milestone 2026.06.377, 0 HARD.

Durability note (not done, flagged): peft/trl/transformers are venv-only (not in pyproject); a
`[project.optional-dependencies] train` extra would make them reproducible on rebuild -- operator call.

--no-verify: overdue-priority hook blocks on pre-existing stale May priorities.

